From bd1fcc10946ae18cd1652af66810e2eb7c7b9191 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OMP Agent <agent@local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:46:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] F-SPLIT-1: expose fail-closed split checkpoint for audit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AblationRunner resolved its split with split_map.get(split, ScenarioSplit.DEV),
so any unrecognised value silently produced a DEV scenario — a fail-open
default in the path that exists to guarantee split integrity. The canonical
label for the validation split is "val", so the 20 call sites passing
split="validation" all ran DEV while intending validation.

The accepted vocabulary is now derived from ScenarioSplit by exact lookup
rather than a duplicated literal map, and resolution happens first in
__init__ so an invalid split raises InvalidScenarioSplit before any run_id,
recorder, or service is constructed. _build_scenario carries a guaranteed
ScenarioSplit member and has no fallback.

Valid behavior is unchanged: dev/val/holdout resolve to the same members and
produce byte-identical run_ids.

The 20 existing "validation" callers are deliberately left unchanged and now
fail loudly. They are the evidence that the invalid vocabulary is in use and
require an operator decision on whether those historical runs were intended
as DEV or as validation.

Adds tests/test_f_split_1_split_vocabulary.py: 74 deterministic tests covering
malformed, forged, non-string, and near-miss inputs; the three valid splits
with exact run_id assertions; and an adversarial control that no invalid input
can yield a DEV scenario or DEV run_id.

EXPECTED FAILURES IN THIS CHECKPOINT
tests/test_run_identity.py reports 6 failures because its helper defaults to
split="validation". These are intentionally NOT repaired. The external auditor
must independently judge three separate questions:

  1. whether the fail-closed change is correct,
  2. whether the test_run_identity failure is expected,
  3. whether the remaining caller/test vocabulary is a distinct issue.

Known results at this commit:
  tests/test_f_split_1_split_vocabulary.py   74 passed
  runner-adjacent suites (10 files)          83 passed, 6 failed
  configured suite (testpaths=tests)       1211 passed, 6 failed

Out of scope and deliberately untouched: split_of(), F1, F4, policy identity,
holdout/evidence/adoption logic, statistical adequacy, C1/C2/C3, Phase 3.
